-- title:
--   Lead coefficients of the weight-2m Hecke image compute T_ℓ^{ss}
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p \ge 5$, an algebraically closed field $K$ of characteristic $p$ with decidable equality, and $N \ge 1$ with $(N : K) \neq 0$; fix a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \neq p$, and an integer $m \ge 1$. Write $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldC K N`, the intermediate field of $K((q))$ generated by the $q$-expansions `jqModC K` and `jqNModC K N`, and $R =$ `charLDegeneracyRoof K N ℓ`, generated by `jqModC K`, `jqNModC K N`, `jqNModC K ℓ` and `jqNModC K (N * ℓ)`; regard $R$ as an $F$-algebra along the inclusion `heckeAlphaC K N ℓ`. Let $h \in R$ satisfy the differential identity $d(\beta(j)) = h \cdot (d j)_R$, where $\beta =$ `heckeBetaC K N ℓ` is the second degeneracy embedding, $j =$ `jGeomGen K N` and $(d j)_R$ is the image of $d j$ under the base-change map of Kähler differentials. Let $G \in F$ lie in the Riemann–Roch space of `weightDivisor K N m` (so $v(G) \le \exp(D v)$ at every place $v$ of $F$ over $K$). Then, assuming also that $T = \ell^{m-1}\,\mathrm{Tr}_{R/F}(\beta(G)\,h^{m})$ lies in that same Riemann–Roch space, for every supersingular index $x \in$ `SSIndex p N K hp5 (2m)` — a place of $F$ in `ssPlaces p N K` whose width divides $m$ — the leading coefficient `lead N K x.1 (poleOrder p N K hp5 (2m) x) T`, i.e. the value at $x$ of $u_x^{e}T$ with $e$ the prescribed pole order, coincides with the value at $x$ of `ssHeckeFun p N K hp5 (2m) ℓ` applied to the supersingular vector $y \mapsto$ `lead N K y.1 (poleOrder p N K hp5 (2m) y) G`.
--
--   This is the function-level commutative square expressing that passing to leading coefficients at the supersingular places intertwines the weight-$2m$ Hecke correspondence $\ell^{m-1}\mathrm{Tr}_{R/F}(\beta(\cdot)h^m)$ on the level-$N$ modular function field with the combinatorially defined supersingular Hecke operator `ssHeckeFun`, whose own recipe uses the semi-local lift `liftFun` of the vector of leading coefficients; the content is thus lift-independence together with the identification of $h$ with `heckeMultiplier N K ℓ`. It is used in establishing the $q$-expansion-level Hecke equivariance `resQFun_heckePS_eq_ssHeckeFun_resQFun` and the window statement `ssHeckeFun_window`.
